From: Kirill =?UTF-8?q?M=C3=BCller?= <kirill@cynkra.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Cast to void * in the default aggregate state initializer

GCC's -Wclass-memaccess fires on every non-trivial STATE_TYPE reaching the
memset fallback of AggregateExecutor::InitializeState. Casting the destination
to void * is the spelling GCC documents for a deliberate raw-byte write; it
states the intent the code already has, and leaves code generation untouched.

---
 .../common/vector_operations/aggregate_executor.hpp     | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/vector_operations/aggregate_executor.hpp b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/vector_operations/aggregate_executor.hpp
index bc1d1318f..6b8b026a4 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/vector_operations/aggregate_executor.hpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/vector_operations/aggregate_executor.hpp
@@ -802,7 +802,7 @@ public:
 		if constexpr (HasInitialize<STATE_TYPE, OP>::value) {
 			OP::Initialize(state);
 		} else {
-			memset(&state, 0, sizeof(STATE_TYPE));
+			memset(static_cast<void *>(&state), 0, sizeof(STATE_TYPE));
 		}
 	}

